# Add a feature to {{ .Name }}

A gox feature module is opted in by importing it and passing its `Enable` option
to `gox.New`. The steps fit all of them; the table below adds the recipe and the
gotchas per feature. Recipes are `docs/recipes/<recipe>.md` in the gox module
directory (AGENTS.md, "Look it up").

## Steps

Features of the root module (outbound HTTP, API keys, translations) have no module
to get and no `Enable` or `From`: follow their recipe, then steps 5 and 6.

1. `go get github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>`. A version like
   `v0.0.0-<date>-<commit>` means the module has no release yet and tracks gox's
   main branch: say so to the user.
{{- if .GoxDir }}
   This service uses a local gox checkout (replace lines in go.mod): add one for
   the new module too, `go mod edit -replace=github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>={{ .GoxDir }}/<module>`.
{{- end }}
2. Read the API for the version you got: `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>`,
   then `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>.<Symbol>`. Read the recipe.
3. Pass `<module>.Enable(...)` to `gox.MustNew` in `cmd/{{ .Name }}/main.go`. Also
   declare `gox.HTTPClient()` for mailgun, s3, stripe and workos: they call out on
   the app's client when it exists (timeouts, tracing, request ids).
4. Read the value with `<module>.From(a)` (openapi and web have none) in `main`
   after `gox.MustNew` and pass it to the feature package:
   `invoices.Register(a, stripe.From(a))`. Handlers never call `From` themselves,
   so tests pass `nil` or a fake.
5. `go run ./cmd/{{ .Name }} --help` lists the new `{{ .Prefix }}_<MODULE>_*` variables.
   Add each one to `.env.example`. Secrets get `mask` when they are fields of your
   own `Config`.
6. `go mod tidy`, then `make test lint`.

## Per feature

| Need | Module | Recipe | Gotchas |
|---|---|---|---|
| JWT bearer tokens | `jwt` | `add-auth` | `jwt.Enable(jwt.WithAuth())` protects every route but `/healthz` and `/readyz`. `gox.WithAuth(jwt.Auth(...))` locks the probes too. For a few routes leave `WithAuth()` off and wrap them with `jwt.Auth(jwt.From(a))`. |
| Tokens from an identity provider (Auth0, Okta, Keycloak, Cognito, Entra) | `jwt` | `verify-identity-provider-tokens` | The issuer variable must equal the tokens' `iss`. A key-set service only verifies; it cannot issue tokens. |
| API keys or opaque tokens | root | `add-auth` (the API-key part at the end) | `middleware.Bearer(validate)` from `pkg/middleware`. Under `gox.WithAuth` it runs for every route, `/healthz` and `/readyz` included: skip those two paths in a wrapper, or wrap only the routes that need it. |
| WorkOS sign-in and sessions | `providers/workos` | `add-workos-login` | `workos.SessionFrom(r)` gives identity, roles and permissions; deciding what they allow stays in the service. `Session.User` is nil for bearer tokens. |
| Enforce an OpenAPI contract | `openapi` | `validate-requests-with-openapi`, `start-from-a-contract` | Pass the auth feature before `openapi.Enable`, or anonymous callers get 400 contract errors instead of 401. `gox.WithAuth` always runs after validation. A `servers` URL with a path (`/api/v1`) prefixes every route: register the full path. |
| Email | `providers/mailgun` | `send-email` | Handlers take a `mail.Sender` (`pkg/mail`): pass `mailgun.Sender(a)`, not `mailgun.From(a)`. Tests pass a `*mail.Recorder`. |
| File storage, uploads | `providers/s3` | `add-file-uploads` | Browsers upload to a presigned URL; the service never proxies the bytes. Handlers take a `storage.Bucket` (`pkg/storage`). MinIO, R2 and other S3-compatible stores set the endpoint variable. |
| Payments, Stripe webhooks | `providers/stripe` | `receive-stripe-webhooks` | `stripe.VerifyWebhook` is the authentication; handle each event id once, Stripe retries until it gets a 2xx. |
| Product analytics, feature flags | `providers/posthog` | `track-events-with-posthog` | A flag lookup error must not fail the request: default the flag. |
| Durable multi-step workflows | `providers/temporal` | `add-temporal-workflow` | Needs a Temporal server; choose it over `gox/jobs` with the gox-background-work skill. |
| Supabase | `providers/supabase` | none | `supabase.From(a)` returns the client; `go doc` is the reference. |
| Translations | root (`pkg/i18n`) | `translate-server-strings` | For strings the server owns (errors, mail, labels). |
| Calls to another HTTP API | root | `call-external-api` | `gox.HTTPClient()` then `a.HTTPClient()`. Retries only for idempotent requests, on a second client from `pkg/httpclient`. Wrap failures: `gox.WrapError(err, gox.CodeUnavailable, "...")`. |
| Durable background jobs | `jobs` | `add-background-job` | Needs Postgres; use the gox-background-work skill. |
{{- if not .Postgres }}
| A Postgres database | `postgres` | `add-migration`, `add-postgres-query` | See "Postgres or pages later" below. |
{{- end }}
{{- if not .Web }}
| Server-rendered HTML pages | `web` | `add-html-page` | See "Postgres or pages later" below. |
{{- end }}

Webhooks from any provider: verify the signature with the provider's
`VerifyWebhook`, answer quickly, and hand slow work to `gox/jobs`.
{{- if .Web }}
With web sessions on, a provider that posts a form (Mailgun inbound mail) is
refused by the CSRF check: add its path prefix to `web.WithCSRFExempt("/webhooks/")`.
JSON posts are never checked.
{{- end }}
{{- if or (not .Postgres) (not .Web) }}

## Postgres or pages later

The scaffold has the wiring. Render a reference copy of this service with every
feature it will have, outside this directory, and copy what the new one adds:

```
go run github.com/guilhermebr/gox/cmd/gox new {{ .Name }} -module {{ .Module }} -postgres -web -dir /tmp/{{ .Name }}-ref
```
{{- if and (not .Postgres) (not .Web) }}

Leave out the flag of a feature you are not adding.
{{- end }}

{{ if not .Postgres -}}
- Postgres: `migrations/`, the `postgres.Enable(postgres.WithMigrations(migrations.FS))`
  option and its import, the POSTGRES lines of `.env.example`.
{{ end -}}
{{ if not .Web -}}
- HTML pages: `web/`, `static/`, `internal/home/` with `home.Register(a)` in place of
  the `GET /{$}` route, the `web.Enable(...)` option and its imports, the
  `github.com/a-h/templ` require line of `go.mod`, the Makefile's templ, htmx and
  Alpine versions and its `generate` and `assets` targets, the WEB lines of
  `.env.example`.
{{ end -}}
- `AGENTS.md` and `.claude/skills/`: replace them with the reference copies (they
  differ per feature), then re-apply your own edits to them.

Then `go mod tidy`{{ if not .Web }}, `make assets`{{ end }} and `make test lint`.
{{- end }}
